# Line endings and binary safety.
#
# core.autocrlf is true here, so git stores LF and hands the working tree CRLF
# on Windows. That is fine for almost everything and NOT fine for one case.

# vitest runs .mjs through vite-node, which passes the source to vm.Script
# largely as-is. With CRLF that throws "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected
# token" on the first line of the module, and vitest reports it against the
# importing test rather than the script — so it reads as a broken test file.
#
# It hid for a while because a freshly written file keeps its LF until git
# next materialises it; the failure only appeared on a branch switch, and would
# have appeared on any clean clone or in CI.
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Never line-ending convert these. Git's binary heuristics already get it
# right, but a mangled GLB or PNG fails in ways that are painful to trace back
# to whitespace, so say it explicitly.
*.glb binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.blend binary
*.zip binary
